# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EPIC ISSUE #509
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
[issue.509]
title = "EPIC: Tax-Lawyer Platform — UFO-grounded multi-jurisdiction R&D/crypto ontology + satisfies constraint system"
status = "open"
labels = ["epic", "tax-lawyer", "ufo", "satisfies", "multi-jurisdiction"]

[issue.509.body]
big_picture = '''
The Tax-Lawyer Platform adds ontologically-grounded tax analysis to the
b00t/l3dg3rr ecosystem. Two architectural currents meet here:

### MCP-down (existing pattern)
ledgrrr publishes 10 MCP tools (ledgerr_tax, ledgerr_evidence, etc.).
The existing pattern: define a Rust enum variant in contract.rs, add a
match arm in mcp_adapter.rs, implement the handler. This PRD extends
ledgerr_tax with 5 new action families (AU R&D eligibility, AU offset
calc, US 4-part test, US credit calc, crypto cost basis).

### UFO-up (new pattern)
A new ufo-types crate grounds every domain concept in a UFO stereotype
(Endurant::SubKind for AuRdActivity, Perdurant::Event for CryptoTx,
Moment::Mode for SatisfiesResult). ISO standard types (LEI, ISO 4217,
ISO 20022, IFRS 9) become the data language. A Satisfies<T> trait
becomes the uniform evaluation pattern — every tax check is
`entity.satisfies::<Constraint>()` returning Blake3-hashed evidence.

### Why both directions are needed
- MCP-down alone produces ad-hoc enums with no shared foundation
  (the previous plan's flaw).
- UFO-up alone produces beautiful types that agents can't call
  (no tool surface).
- Together: UFO-up gives ontological rigor + ISO standards + audit trail.
  MCP-down gives agent-accessible tool surface. The Satisfies trait is
  the bridge — it produces evidence nodes in arc-kit-au that are
  discoverable through ledgerr_evidence MCP tools.

### Issue dependency graph
  #510 (foundation) → #511 (AU R&D) ─┐
                   → #512 (US R&D)  ─┤ → #514 (MCP layer)
                   → #513 (crypto)  ─┘
  #515 (skills) is independent (content only, ships immediately)

### Definition of epic done
  - crates/ufo-types exists with UFO categories, Satisfies trait, ISO types
  - ledger-core has AuRdActivity, QreExpenditure, CryptoTx with satisfies impls
  - ledgerr_mcp contract.rs has all 5 new action families
  - All handlers are thin wrappers (≤10 lines, no domain logic)
  - regen-docs produces no diff
  - 9 SKILL.md files exist under skills/tax-lawyer/
  - End-to-end: agent calls ledgerr_tax → satisfies → evidence graph → audit trail
'''

